WEBVTT

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:15.370
Sebastian Moran is holding
a charity concert to support

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:19.250
those on the East Side
who've done so much for us.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.870
This is our main guest!

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.910
"Masaya"

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.500
I hope to see you all there!

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.410
Forget that, tell us
about Tony Shigeru's article!

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:32.700
Is it true that there're ties between
Mayor Moran and Jack the Ripper?

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.580
That article is lies.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.580
I believe in my father.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:45.120
This concludes the conference.
Everyone, please leave immediately.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:49.000
Is the concert a way to bring up
his flagging poll numbers?

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.000
Tell us more, James- <i>san</i> !

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:25.040
"The Curtain Rises on the Grand Guignol"

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.660
The line forms here!

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.700
"Shinjuku East Side Stadium"

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:32.370
Mrs. Hudson, the goddess
of Kabukicho, will be singing, too!

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.580
Look forward to it!

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:39.000
So lame.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.120
Sherlock made all the stuff for Mrs. Hudson.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.540
That explains it.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:49.500
"The Legendary Fugu Lunch
Just pull the string for a piping hot meal!"

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.620
Let me see your ticket.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:50.910
Here you go.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:54.580
Thanks, mister.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:59.580
The legendary Fugu Lunch
will be given to all participants!

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:06.660
It's all powerful people from the East Side.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:10.410
Only the seat to Mayor Moran's left is empty.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.580
Security reasons?

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:21.200
Mayor Moran! Mayor Moran!

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.290
We have questions!

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:30.040
Looks like that article's
still having an effect.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:34.450
Head to the West Side
Shinjuku Ward Office immediately!

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:38.370
Repeat: Head to the West Side
Shinjuku Ward Office immediately!

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.370
Yes. Yes.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.330
Understood.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.830
A bomb was found in the Ward Office!

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.790
I see.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:56.000
We're not going?

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.950
There's no need to go there.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:02.160
The bomb is somewhere here in the stadium.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.620
"Three Days Earlier"

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:10.620
To my beloved Sebastian Moran,

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.950
The curtain has risen on the Grand Guignol.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:16.410
When a single flower blooms
on the bloodstained stage,

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:20.540
your hopes will be shattered into dust.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:24.000
From Albert Trevor, with love.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.370
What's this?

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:27.450
Some lunatic?

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:30.750
Albert? The leader of the escapees?

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:35.620
Yeah. A bomber responsible
for several major bombings.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:39.750
The casualties from his bombs
reach into the hundreds.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.950
So this is a bomb threat?

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:47.160
This was delivered to the
Moran residence last night.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:52.160
I want you to find Trevor and
catch him before the bomb goes off.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:55.120
I went to the police, but...

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:56.500
Sorry, everyone.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.620
The media's watching me and I can't go.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:01.450
I want you to do the investigation for me!

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:04.080
You're all I can count on!

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.250
Please, everyone!

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:11.950
James- <i>sama</i> insisted on using you.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:16.250
We'll pay your expenses
as well as 50,000,000 yen.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:20.330
We know where the bomb will be set.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:25.160
The charity concert.

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:30.870
Welcome to my charity concert, everyone!

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:33.370
Hey, how can you be sure it's here?

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:33.390
"Stadium - Nosebleed Seats"

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:39.660
Albert is the type of criminal who loves
attention more than anything else.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:40.620
Let's see...

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:44.250
Where has he set bombs before?

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:47.080
Sky Tower? Diamond Bridge?

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:50.330
Yeah, these are all famous places
with loads of people.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:54.870
He wouldn't choose the
Ward Office on a day it's closed.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:53.330
"Stadium - Arena"

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:56.290
"Middle Seats"

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:58.330
It was a trap to lure away the police.

00:05:56.700 --> 00:06:01.210
"Stadium - Arena"

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:01.250
This is what he's after!

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.870
I hope you'll all enjoy yourselves!

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:14.330
It's now time for Mayor Sebastian
Moran's charity concert!

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:15.640
"Stadium - North Stand Lower Deck"

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:17.620
Huh? Why isn't it getting warmer?

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:22.790
"Let's begin the game, detectives."

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:22.790
What's this?

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:25.950
"Let's begin the game, detectives"?

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:30.120
"Pitch black stars scattered in a vast space..."

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:34.200
"One of them holds a
morning star filled with flame."

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:37.120
"Find the morning star and you win.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.830
If you can't, I win."

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:45.580
"The morning star will ignite
if you evacuate the stadium."

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:48.040
Does he mean the bomb?

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.700
We need to find it now.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:52.580
Look at the audience.

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:56.580
Black stars?

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:01.290
We have to find the bomb from one of these?

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:03.290
It's the lunches, everyone!

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:05.580
One of the lunches is the bomb!

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:08.660
This is...

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:13.540
Wait, my lunch didn't...!

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:22.700
If it didn't warm up that means that
something was done to the warmer...

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:32.500
"Nope"

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:36.160
Aww, no way.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:37.330
It's true!

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:39.700
The lunches have marks on them.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:41.870
He's done something to the warmers.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:44.290
Some of them are misses!

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:45.450
Really!

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:47.370
Why don't you come with us?

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:49.290
Wow, I'm down!

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:53.450
I don't hear anything.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.250
You're not opening it, sis?

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:59.040
Hey, if it's the bomb...

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:07.500
"The backbone of a heavenly palace.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:11.200
Waiting at its tail end is a forbidden
closet wreathed in crimson,

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:14.700
and a man with a magic key."

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:18.450
Heavenly palace... tail end...

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:18.450
Is this a hint to the bomb?

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:21.200
Crimson. Closet. Key.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.830
Bluebeard.

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:26.950
The back seats. Lower decks.

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:28.540
A bearded man in red.

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:33.790
I don't have time for riddles.

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:36.450
I'll just use good old fashioned shoe leather.

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:39.700
Um, excuse me. Excuse me.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:42.370
I'm with the health department.

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:47.450
There was a problem with your lunches...

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:49.290
"Nope"

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:56.910
I know this next one...

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:04.250
I guess this is another miss.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:07.700
Give me your lunch!

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:10.700
What's your problem!

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:11.830
Sorry!

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:17.200
Jeez. What's wrong?

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:20.540
The man in red's lunch wasn't the bomb.

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:26.210
"On the night when Polaris shines,
the bell sounds at midnight,
and a bambino smiles with a vessel
holding the sky in his hand."

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:27.450
Next, north stands, upper decks.

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:29.580
A child with a balloon.

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:33.830
Found it!

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:36.590
"Stadium - North Stand Upper Decks"

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:35.580
What do we do?

00:09:35.580 --> 00:09:36.910
Calm down!

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:41.120
It's a time bomb of simple construction.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:45.200
We remove the cover and slice
the wire leading to the sensor.

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:50.450
And then all that's left is to cut
either the red or blue wire.

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:51.540
You're shitting me.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:53.620
Which one?

00:09:53.620 --> 00:10:00.160
My detective's intuition
tells me to cut this one!

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.330
Damn it!

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:08.750
Is Albert playing with us?

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:11.160
Next one: main stand upper decks!

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:12.870
Lady with a black umbrella!

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:14.420
"Stadium - Main Stand Upper Decks"

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:16.870
South stand, lower decks!

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:18.790
Twins in blue!

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:20.040
Which one?

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:21.090
"South Stand Lower Decks"

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:21.410
Both!

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:25.870
Next!

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:27.450
No dice!

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:33.730
"Nope"

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:37.040
I've lost track of how many I've opened!

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:41.870
How can I not find it when
I've solved the riddles?

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:44.540
I'll draw a line between
the places he pointed out...

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:48.200
Is there some meaning left in the riddles?

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:55.830
Hope will be shattered.

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:58.580
What is Moran's hope?

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:02.910
Thank you.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:05.540
And now...

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.870
When the sun sets in other towns,

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:11.910
in our town the neon lights turn on.

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:15.870
Our last act for the day
is someone you all know.

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:19.410
The former legendary host of Kabukicho!

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.830
Masaya!

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:29.250
"Singer"

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:35.120
♪ Half a man speaking of half of a dream. ♪

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:42.540
♪ He says he's never coming back... ♪

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:46.000
"The mad banquet comes to an end.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:49.580
The shining star's singing
heralds the end of the game.

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:53.250
When it ends, the morning star will light."

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:55.330
The end of singing...

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:57.330
Does that mean the bomb goes off

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:59.580
when Masaya's song is over...?

00:12:00.790 --> 00:12:06.200
♪ As we strain for one last look... ♪

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:07.870
What do we do, Sherlock?

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:11.660
Everyone will die!

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.540
That's right.

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:26.000
"South Stand"

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:23.410
It's me. Come to the back of the south stand.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:38.790
What's wrong, Sherlock?

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:41.290
Did you find the bomb?

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:42.370
No.

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:45.450
I see.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:48.660
You're behind this, Moriarty.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.160
Why's that?

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:55.700
And not just this.

00:12:55.700 --> 00:13:00.620
Isshiki. Dopey. Saizo. The girls.

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:05.290
The ones who made it out
of the prison committed crimes

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:07.330
and then killed themselves.

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:10.370
You were controlling it all.

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.500
You didn't answer with a joke?

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:18.660
That's so dull.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:24.660
Yup. I was behind it all.

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:32.450
Not that I was "controlling" anybody.

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:35.000
I just talked to them a little,

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:41.620
bringing out the desires
and greed within their hearts.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:47.620
This bomb threat, for example,
was what Albert really wanted to do.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:49.950
Mind control.

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:53.450
And you put a hypnotic suggestion
on them to commit suicide

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:54.870
when they were of no use.

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:58.830
The trigger was their own name, wasn't it?

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:00.870
Smart, Sherlock!

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:03.040
You figured it out.

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:08.410
You set them up to die when the
cops called them by their full name.

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:13.080
Something like that.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:16.410
That number they whispered before they died.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:17.500
What was that?

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:20.500
Oh, like a special stamp.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:23.250
I gave it to the ones I liked.

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:28.700
So, you actually figured out
where the bomb is, right?

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:30.250
Tell me already.

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:32.450
Come on, one, two...

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:35.500
No.

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:37.040
What do you mean?

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:42.160
I lose.

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:46.750
I admit defeat.

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:49.750
Stop Albert.

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:51.200
Please.

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:58.290
Shit! It's over!

00:14:58.290 --> 00:14:59.790
Sis!

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:06.120
Time for an encore!

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:17.580
You want to stop it that badly.

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:22.660
Kiss my shoes then, Sherlock.

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:39.660
That's not what you're supposed to do!

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:46.450
Stop it!

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:54.040
You heard it all, huh?

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:55.830
Yeah.

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:59.000
Moriarty, why?

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:02.080
'Cause it's fun, of course!

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:04.790
Fun?

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:06.910
What're you so surprised about?

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:08.410
It wasn't just me.

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:11.830
Sherlock had a good time, too, I bet!

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:14.000
What do you mean?

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:17.790
You really don't understand a thing.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:24.330
Sherlock figured out I was
behind it a long time ago.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:26.620
He suspected me for so long.

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:27.950
Watched me.

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:31.660
And at the zoo he was sure.

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:33.870
Right, Sherlock?

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:38.910
But you didn't call the cops.

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:42.000
Or stop me. You didn't do a thing.

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:46.200
Why? Because you were having fun.

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:50.830
You were excited to see
what would happen next, right?

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:55.580
Sherlock...

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:57.580
He's lying, right?

00:16:57.580 --> 00:16:59.580
It's all lies, right?

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:05.580
Tell me, Sherlock!

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:08.160
No.

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:09.790
No...

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:14.000
But there's one thing I didn't like.

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:18.910
When I watched him solve the case...

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:23.000
It felt like he'd become boring.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.870
So I decided to test him!

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:29.620
That was the goal of today's bomb hunting game!

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:32.790
Albert sent the bomb threat at the perfect time,

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:34.700
so I decided to take advantage of it.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:39.620
I distributed the altered lunches
and sent messages to your pagers.

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:42.750
Oh, those messages were fakes.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:45.830
Solving them won't help you.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:48.620
The old Sherlock would've

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:55.830
kept solving the mystery until the
bombs went off, even if people died.

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:59.000
Unfortunately, he failed the test.

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:01.330
But there's still time.

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:02.370
What?

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:04.250
If you really wanted to stop me,

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:06.330
you would've at least brought Watson.

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:11.040
But you came to see me alone
without telling him.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:17.370
In some part of your heart,
you wanted to continue the game.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:22.660
So I'm giving you a make-up test.

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:29.500
Come with me, Sherlock.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:31.410
I'll introduce you to Albert.

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:34.370
We can have even more fun together.

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:40.200
Can you make him stop the bomb?

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:41.700
Sure.

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:50.200
Don't go!

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:52.080
I'm here!

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:54.040
So's the rest of the row house!

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:58.250
So don't go, Sherlock!

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:00.660
Or I'll...

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:04.290
I'll get mad!

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:09.750
Stand up! Or I'll get mad, James!

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:24.200
So what Alex is to me, Watson is to you, huh?

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:27.540
Thank you, everyone!

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:30.620
See you later!

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:37.450
Detectives, it seems I've won the game!

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:41.080
Hello to all of you attending the concert.

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:43.700
I am Albert Trevor.

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:48.200
It's time for the finale of the Grand Guignol!

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:52.000
A brilliant flower!

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:03.540
Moriarty!

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:10.910
Moriarty said he used the bomb threat
as an excuse to set up the bomb hunt.

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:13.620
Sherlock, there isn't time!

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:18.330
So Albert's bomb isn't part of the game?

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:20.080
That's right.

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:24.040
Looking at what Moriarty did in today's chaos...

00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:27.330
Albert's only message was the first threat!

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:31.830
"A single flower"

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:28.700
Correct.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:31.830
There was only one bomb.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:39.250
"On the night when Polaris shines, the bell sounds
at midnight, and a bambino smiles
with a vessel holding the sky in his hand.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:35.410
But there's plenty going off now!

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:39.450
Those are probably fakes planted by Moriarty.

00:20:39.450 --> 00:20:42.830
Where's the real firework?

00:20:42.830 --> 00:20:46.290
What is Moran's hope?

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:50.500
"Masaya"

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:50.500
"I Love Masaya"

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:52.330
I found it.

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:54.410
He's after...

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:59.500
I'm sorry about all this, Godain- <i>sama</i> !

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:59.520
"Godain Construction CEO"

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:09.540
Calm this down.

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:11.790
And hold a press conference...

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:26.080
My black story, my Grand Guignol, is complete!

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:14.290
Do you want to know how I created this story?

00:23:14.290 --> 00:23:16.700
I shall tell you.

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:20.870
A single message was sent to Sebastian Moran...

00:23:20.870 --> 00:23:24.660
The story had begun.

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:24.660
Good work, Albert.

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:28.290
Let me begin by telling you
about the Grand Guignol.

00:23:28.290 --> 00:23:34.620
In 1897, the author Oscar Méténier

00:23:28.950 --> 00:23:33.330
Mary! Mary!

00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:34.620
Where are you, Mary?

00:23:34.620 --> 00:23:38.080
Mary!

00:23:34.620 --> 00:23:40.330
remodeled an empty Parsian
chapel into a theater...

00:23:38.080 --> 00:23:40.330
Can you do me another favor?

00:23:40.330 --> 00:23:44.910
This theater would later be known for its...

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:49.940
"Moriarty Savors"

00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:47.450
What are you after?

00:23:47.450 --> 00:23:49.910
You know the answer to that.

00:23:49.940 --> 00:23:51.950
"Shinjuku's Miracle Prince, and the last
super star of the age, makes his singing debut!"
"Debut Song: 'Two Cranes in the Fog Masaya'"
"The two cranes are a metaphor for our love."
